# Spend you can cap

```elixir
Mix.install([{:wardrik, "~> 0.1.0-rc.2"}, {:kino, "~> 0.19"}])
```

## What a call costs

Wardrik prices model calls from the catalog, in dollars per million tokens:

```elixir
{:ok, haiku} = ReqLLM.model("anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5")

# 400 tokens in, 700 out
(400 * haiku.cost.input + 700 * haiku.cost.output) / 1_000_000
```

A dollar budget denies a model with no price. Give one with Wardrik's `:prices` option.

## A budget on paper

```elixir
asks = WardrikPolicy.new!(budget: [usd: 0.01, per: :day]).budget
denies = WardrikPolicy.new!(budget: [usd: 0.01, per: :day, on_exhausted: :deny]).budget

for usd <- [0.004, 0.009, 0.012] do
  %{
    spent: usd,
    asks: WardrikPolicy.Budget.check(asks, %{usd: usd}),
    denies: WardrikPolicy.Budget.check(denies, %{usd: usd})
  }
end
```

- The call that crosses the limit runs.
- `on_exhausted: :ask`, the default, makes the next call wait. Approving allows another limit's worth.
- `on_exhausted: :deny` refuses it.

## Setup

Add `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the Secrets panel. This spends about three cents.

```elixir
System.put_env("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", System.fetch_env!("LB_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"))

defmodule MyApp.AllowAll do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Authorizer
  def authorize(_request, _opts), do: :ok
end

defmodule MyApp.Agents do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Resolver
  def resolve(_request, _opts), do: {:ok, %Wardrik.Resolved{principal: Wardrik.principal("maria")}}
end

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.start_link(
    name: MyApp.AgentRuntime,
    authorizer: {MyApp.AllowAll, []},
    resolver: {MyApp.Agents, []}
  )

scope = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "maria")

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.Agent.define(scope, "agt_writer",
    model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5",
    instructions: "You write short stories about office life.",
    policy: [budget: [usd: 0.01, per: :day]]
  )

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.Agent.define(scope, "agt_editor",
    model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5",
    instructions: "You write short memos about office life.",
    policy: [budget: [usd: 0.01, per: :day, on_exhausted: :deny]]
  )
```

## Live spend

```elixir
rows = fn ->
  {:ok, agents} = Wardrik.Agents.list(scope)

  for agent <- agents,
      do: %{agent: agent.id, status: agent.status, usd: agent.spent_today["usd"]}
end

table = Kino.DataTable.new(rows.(), name: "Agents today", keys: [:agent, :status, :usd])
Kino.listen(1_000, fn _tick -> Kino.DataTable.update(table, rows.()) end)
table
```

## The writer asks

```elixir
ask = fn agent, what ->
  Enum.reduce_while(1..10, nil, fn n, _ ->
    case Wardrik.Agent.reply(scope, agent, "Write #{what} #{n}, in about 300 words.") do
      {:ok, _reply} -> {:cont, n}
      stopped -> {:halt, stopped}
    end
  end)
end

ask.("agt_writer", "story")
```

It waits on a `:model_approval`. Allow another cent:

```elixir
Wardrik.Agent.approve(scope, agent: "agt_writer", interrupt: "model")
```

## The editor is refused

```elixir
ask.("agt_editor", "memo")
```

The run fails with the budget's message.

